  "question": {
    "text": "Two polaroids have their polarizing directions parallel so that the intensity of a transmitted light is maximum. The angle through which either polaroid must be turned if the intensity is to drop by one-half is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "X5Xvy",
      "text": "\n$135^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "y3jKL",
      "text": "\n$90^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "q3HCN",
      "text": "\n$120^{\\circ}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QZhj8",
      "text": "\n$180^{\\circ}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $I=\\frac{I_0}{2}$ and $I=I_0 \\cos ^2 \\theta=\\frac{I_0}{2}$ $\\therefore \\theta=45^{\\circ}$\nTherefore the angle through which either polaroids turned is $135^{\\circ}\\left(=180^{\\circ}-45^{\\circ}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
